    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44357" root="&#xA;                        همل&#xA;                    " body-key="h1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَمَلَ</span></b> 
                        , aor. 
    
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَمُلَ</span></b> 
                        , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَمَلاَنٌ</span>; and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اِنْهَمَلَ</span></b> ;
<i>It</i> (water) <i>overflowed, and poured forth.</i> (Mgh.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُهْمَلُ عَلَى رُؤُوسِهَا وَظَهُورِهَا</span>; so in a copy of
the K, voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسُوطٌ</span>: in other copies of the K,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُحْمَلُ</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُحْمَلُ</span>: if the first be correct, the
meaning is probably Camels <i>left without rein
and without burden;</i> and this is agreeable with
the context.

